1
00:00:00,370 --> 00:00:01,740
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,740 --> 00:00:03,210
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:04,610 --> 00:00:06,040
(Episode 24)

4
00:00:07,710 --> 00:00:08,750
Right.

5
00:00:09,550 --> 00:00:11,280
I'll do my part,

6
00:00:12,180 --> 00:00:14,320
so make sure you do your part
someday too.

7
00:00:22,830 --> 00:00:24,330
I'm not giving up on this.

8
00:00:25,460 --> 00:00:28,270
Whether it's Paris or New York,
design school is...

9
00:00:29,430 --> 00:00:30,840
definitely not something
I'm giving up on.

10
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:33,100
I'm just postponing it
for a while...

11
00:00:34,710 --> 00:00:36,240
(Haedeul Bank)

12
00:00:36,310 --> 00:00:37,880
to protect my family.

13
00:00:48,290 --> 00:00:50,360
(Sibling 2)

14
00:00:55,690 --> 00:00:57,300
- Come out.
- What?

15
00:00:58,230 --> 00:00:59,930
What do you mean, come out?
Where are you?

16
00:01:00,730 --> 00:01:02,900
I'm in front of your office,
so come out right now.

17
00:01:05,270 --> 00:01:06,300
My office?

18
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:08,170
Are you really in front
of my office? Really?

19
00:01:09,110 --> 00:01:10,480
I told you I am.

20
00:01:10,610 --> 00:01:12,110
Come out
while I'm still feeling generous.

21
00:01:12,680 --> 00:01:14,950
Really? Kkangda, are you serious?

22
00:01:15,410 --> 00:01:16,510
You're not lying, right?

23
00:01:18,380 --> 00:01:20,590
Come out if you want to get
your money, you fool.

24
00:01:24,460 --> 00:01:26,520
(Haedeul Bank)

25
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:37,270
Hurry up and run here, Kang Dae Chi,

26
00:01:38,970 --> 00:01:40,740
before your dear sister
changes her mind.

27
00:01:42,440 --> 00:01:43,810
Gosh, wait...

28
00:01:45,410 --> 00:01:46,440
Wait a second.

29
00:01:47,610 --> 00:01:49,580
What if that cheapskate
is acting all dramatic...

30
00:01:49,580 --> 00:01:50,920
just to hand me 5,000 dollars?

31
00:01:52,020 --> 00:01:54,990
No, 5,000 dollars is better
than nothing in my situation.

32
00:01:59,520 --> 00:02:01,990
Mr. Kang Dae Chi,
since we haven't received your payment,

33
00:02:01,990 --> 00:02:03,530
I'm sending this text message.

34
00:02:03,600 --> 00:02:06,030
If payment is not confirmed
by midnight today,

35
00:02:06,030 --> 00:02:10,840
we will assume you have no intention
of repaying your debt to us.

36
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:11,840
Darn it.

37
00:02:12,540 --> 00:02:13,870
(Hwanggeum Brat)

38
00:02:17,140 --> 00:02:19,540
I will pay it.
I'll pay the three months of interest.

39
00:02:19,610 --> 00:02:22,150
So please, don't come
to my office or home, okay?

40
00:02:22,480 --> 00:02:24,820
Never ever show up here,
do you hear me?

41
00:02:25,020 --> 00:02:26,650
Do you understand?

42
00:02:27,820 --> 00:02:29,150
My ears.

43
00:02:31,590 --> 00:02:33,690
Yes, sir. I'll trust you, then.

44
00:02:33,690 --> 00:02:36,330
Please make sure
to transfer it today.

45
00:02:40,130 --> 00:02:42,370
Still, if one visit got me
three months of interest,

46
00:02:42,370 --> 00:02:43,600
I might actually have
a knack for this.

47
00:02:46,170 --> 00:02:47,840
Did he say he'd pay today?

48
00:02:48,170 --> 00:02:50,740
Well...
Yes, he asked me to trust him.

49
00:02:51,080 --> 00:02:53,040
Everyone says that.

50
00:02:56,180 --> 00:02:58,820
- Just empty words?
- People who actually prove it...

51
00:02:58,880 --> 00:02:59,950
are rare these days.

52
00:03:06,420 --> 00:03:07,430
Either that...

53
00:03:07,730 --> 00:03:10,400
or they make you want to trust them
just a little bit longer.

54
00:03:17,770 --> 00:03:18,900
(Name: Manager Kang Da Mi
Phone: 010-0928-0331)

55
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:35,290
Right. I took her to the flea market
and taught her. That's enough.

56
00:03:35,290 --> 00:03:36,390
Why do more?

57
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:57,510
This is precious to you, right?

58
00:04:09,190 --> 00:04:10,990
(Organza, Chiffon)

59
00:04:11,490 --> 00:04:12,620
(Keep the overall silhouette,
but reduce the frills' weight!)

60
00:04:23,700 --> 00:04:25,470
What's this guy doing?

61
00:04:26,200 --> 00:04:27,710
Is he busy
trying to earn overtime pay...

62
00:04:27,770 --> 00:04:29,510
since he's buried in debt?

63
00:04:31,180 --> 00:04:32,940
I'm starving.

64
00:04:33,710 --> 00:04:36,610
Emptying my savings
just makes me feel even hungrier.

65
00:04:38,220 --> 00:04:40,220
I'm feeling chilly
for no reason, too.

66
00:04:45,690 --> 00:04:47,590
Are you out of your mind?
Don't you want your money?

67
00:04:47,660 --> 00:04:48,990
I'm just going home.

68
00:04:52,430 --> 00:04:54,030
I told you to come out quickly.

69
00:04:54,100 --> 00:04:56,370
Are you in any position
to keep me waiting, Your Highness?

70
00:04:57,900 --> 00:04:58,900
Excuse me.

71
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:02,040
Are you busy working overtime?
Should I come up?

72
00:05:02,740 --> 00:05:03,880
Excuse me, but...

73
00:05:04,280 --> 00:05:06,240
isn't this
Manager Kang Da Mi's phone?

74
00:05:10,150 --> 00:05:13,320
Oh, goodness. Hello, sir.

75
00:05:13,380 --> 00:05:15,150
This is Manager Kang Da Mi.

76
00:05:15,590 --> 00:05:19,490
I'm sorry,
but may I ask who is calling?

77
00:05:20,730 --> 00:05:21,730
This is Cha Seung Yun.

78
00:05:22,230 --> 00:05:23,460
Pardon? Who did you say you were?

79
00:05:24,300 --> 00:05:25,630
Cha Seung Yun.

80
00:05:26,230 --> 00:05:29,430
The one who took my tablet...

81
00:05:30,170 --> 00:05:31,200
It wasn't me.

82
00:05:31,270 --> 00:05:34,470
My younger sister took it
by mistake, thinking it was hers,

83
00:05:34,470 --> 00:05:36,940
and I personally returned it to you.

84
00:05:37,640 --> 00:05:41,280
Yes, sir. So what is this regarding?

85
00:05:41,350 --> 00:05:42,780
There's something
I want to give you.

86
00:05:42,850 --> 00:05:44,820
Hey, Da Mi! Kang Da Mi!

87
00:05:45,980 --> 00:05:48,250
Sir, I'm sorry.
I'm currently outside,

88
00:05:48,350 --> 00:05:49,950
and the background noise
is making it hard to...

89
00:05:51,260 --> 00:05:52,260
Hello?

90
00:05:52,620 --> 00:05:53,620
Hello...

91
00:05:54,390 --> 00:05:55,390
Have you been waiting long?

92
00:05:55,830 --> 00:05:57,160
I had to meet an employee
from a client company...

93
00:05:57,160 --> 00:05:58,500
nearby for a moment.

94
00:05:59,660 --> 00:06:00,730
You haven't eaten dinner, right?

95
00:06:01,300 --> 00:06:02,800
Shall we go inside somewhere
to talk?

96
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:05,170
From now on, both of us are broke.

97
00:06:05,500 --> 00:06:06,770
Let's talk over there.

98
00:06:06,770 --> 00:06:08,040
We can't afford to go
sit inside anywhere.

99
00:06:09,040 --> 00:06:10,070
What?

100
00:06:10,780 --> 00:06:12,610
Okay, sure.

101
00:06:15,450 --> 00:06:16,450
"Your Highness"?

102
00:06:19,320 --> 00:06:20,590
Do people use
that kind of expression nowadays?

103
00:06:24,060 --> 00:06:25,190
Well, there will be another chance.

104
00:06:28,330 --> 00:06:29,330
Yes?

105
00:06:30,830 --> 00:06:32,400
- Not asleep yet?
- Grandma.

106
00:06:32,460 --> 00:06:33,630
Yes, it's me.

107
00:06:34,400 --> 00:06:35,400
Yes.

108
00:06:36,300 --> 00:06:38,040
What's this?

109
00:06:38,840 --> 00:06:41,640
Did I disturb your work?

110
00:06:41,940 --> 00:06:44,010
- Not at all.
- Okay.

111
00:06:44,340 --> 00:06:46,980
I wanted to come down earlier
and chat with you, Grandma.

112
00:06:47,210 --> 00:06:49,510
But the mood today
didn't seem right,

113
00:06:49,580 --> 00:06:51,120
so we all stayed upstairs
on the second floor.

114
00:06:51,850 --> 00:06:54,620
I see. I made you worry.

115
00:06:54,690 --> 00:06:56,850
No, it wasn't that.
Please sit down, Grandma.

116
00:06:56,850 --> 00:06:57,860
Okay.

117
00:06:58,760 --> 00:06:59,820
All right.

118
00:07:06,100 --> 00:07:10,030
Yes. Seung Yun, tomorrow is...

119
00:07:10,370 --> 00:07:11,670
I know what day it is.

120
00:07:12,470 --> 00:07:14,570
Will you go visit tomorrow?

121
00:07:15,840 --> 00:07:17,910
Yes, I plan to go in the morning.

122
00:07:18,280 --> 00:07:19,280
Okay.

123
00:07:19,940 --> 00:07:22,210
All right, get some rest early.

124
00:07:23,010 --> 00:07:24,550
Grandma, let me walk down with you.

125
00:07:24,750 --> 00:07:28,320
It's all right.
I can go down by myself.

126
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:30,120
Oh, right.

127
00:07:31,890 --> 00:07:35,330
If you see Dr. Ju
when you go tomorrow,

128
00:07:35,890 --> 00:07:38,330
ask him to buy you a meal, okay?

129
00:07:39,300 --> 00:07:40,770
- Dr. Ju?
- Yes.

130
00:07:40,770 --> 00:07:42,800
Why would Dr. Ju
be at the columbarium?

131
00:07:43,100 --> 00:07:44,240
He'll treat you.

132
00:07:46,970 --> 00:07:48,610
- Okay.
- Yes.

133
00:07:50,470 --> 00:07:51,480
All right.

134
00:07:54,280 --> 00:07:56,250
- That's enough.
- Okay. Take care on your way down.

135
00:07:56,310 --> 00:07:57,320
Yes.

136
00:08:03,350 --> 00:08:04,520
Dr. Ju tomorrow?

137
00:08:09,290 --> 00:08:11,230
(Cashier's Check 200,000 Dollars)

138
00:08:13,600 --> 00:08:15,200
What? Hey.

139
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:17,400
My little sister...

140
00:08:19,170 --> 00:08:21,470
Now you finally call me
your little sister.

141
00:08:23,770 --> 00:08:24,780
Hey, come on.

142
00:08:25,040 --> 00:08:27,510
Has there ever been a time
when you weren't my little sister?

143
00:08:32,880 --> 00:08:33,890
Still...

144
00:08:35,320 --> 00:08:38,220
Are you going to be okay...

145
00:08:40,260 --> 00:08:41,260
after lending me
over 200,000 dollars?

146
00:08:42,660 --> 00:08:44,130
I can take care of myself.

147
00:08:44,630 --> 00:08:47,370
So please,
just get your own act together.

148
00:08:48,600 --> 00:08:50,130
I used to do just fine.

149
00:08:52,300 --> 00:08:53,570
I just slipped up once.

150
00:08:54,670 --> 00:08:57,310
Slipped up?
If you had broken a bone,

151
00:08:57,440 --> 00:08:58,780
you would've blown up
the entire planet.

152
00:09:03,510 --> 00:09:05,220
I'm sorry.
I've been a terrible brother.

153
00:09:06,650 --> 00:09:07,920
By the time you get married,

154
00:09:08,820 --> 00:09:10,660
I'll definitely pay all of it back.

155
00:09:11,190 --> 00:09:12,890
I'm not even dreaming of interest.

156
00:09:13,620 --> 00:09:16,730
Consider it a family discount
and just pay back the principal.

157
00:09:16,930 --> 00:09:17,930
Got it?

158
00:09:18,500 --> 00:09:19,560
Got it.

159
00:09:22,870 --> 00:09:24,740
By the way, you're not
seeing anyone right now, are you?

160
00:09:24,740 --> 00:09:26,770
You don't have a crush
on anyone, do you?

161
00:09:27,240 --> 00:09:31,780
I'll get married just to get
my money back from you,

162
00:09:32,140 --> 00:09:33,510
so stop daydreaming...

163
00:09:33,580 --> 00:09:35,750
and just focus on working hard
at that company, understand?

164
00:09:36,610 --> 00:09:37,680
Did you hear me?

165
00:09:38,320 --> 00:09:39,480
I heard you.

166
00:09:41,690 --> 00:09:42,690
I'll do my best.

167
00:09:44,620 --> 00:09:46,560
And make sure you keep your promise.

168
00:09:47,460 --> 00:09:49,330
Don't tell anyone in our family...

169
00:09:49,390 --> 00:09:51,530
a single word
about me giving you this money.

170
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:54,200
Especially to Mom.
Don't show any sign of it.

171
00:09:56,670 --> 00:09:57,670
Okay.

172
00:09:58,240 --> 00:09:59,370
Let's go.

173
00:10:00,440 --> 00:10:01,570
- Right.
- What a day...

174
00:10:06,880 --> 00:10:07,880
What?

175
00:10:08,780 --> 00:10:10,650
Want me to carry your bag?

176
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:13,120
I'll carry it. I was just about to.

177
00:10:14,050 --> 00:10:15,350
I told you not to act obvious,
didn't I?

178
00:10:16,750 --> 00:10:18,620
No one is watching, you brat.

179
00:10:19,020 --> 00:10:20,020
Brat?

180
00:10:20,990 --> 00:10:23,490
Okay, sorry.
I'll be careful from now on.

181
00:10:24,700 --> 00:10:25,830
Let's go home, little sis.

182
00:10:47,080 --> 00:10:49,150
Don't be so upset.

183
00:10:51,190 --> 00:10:52,190
At least this time...

184
00:10:52,420 --> 00:10:55,830
I'm the only one who lost points.
You didn't lose any.

185
00:10:57,860 --> 00:11:00,800
You saw that she was
only scolding me, didn't you?

186
00:11:01,470 --> 00:11:04,400
Let's just be glad
we didn't both lose points, okay?

187
00:11:05,270 --> 00:11:07,770
That makes me feel even worse.

188
00:11:08,810 --> 00:11:10,710
Why? What do you mean?

189
00:11:11,210 --> 00:11:12,740
You know how she is.

190
00:11:13,010 --> 00:11:17,720
Mother isn't the type to let
even the slightest mistake slide by.

191
00:11:18,380 --> 00:11:22,020
If she had gotten mad at me instead,
I'd feel much better.

192
00:11:23,490 --> 00:11:24,490
This just means...

193
00:11:25,120 --> 00:11:26,790
she's simply ignoring me.

194
00:11:27,560 --> 00:11:30,460
She doesn't even consider me worth
getting angry at.

195
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:40,000
Honey.

196
00:11:40,670 --> 00:11:42,170
Cut back on your work.

197
00:11:42,770 --> 00:11:44,510
You're just overworked.

198
00:11:44,780 --> 00:11:48,010
Overthinking like this
only proves how exhausted you are.

199
00:11:49,550 --> 00:11:51,350
I'm not making a fuss over nothing.

200
00:11:51,850 --> 00:11:54,290
How does it make any sense
to remove you as CEO...

201
00:11:54,290 --> 00:11:56,620
just because one PR article
went out wrong?

202
00:11:57,620 --> 00:11:59,890
And the timing is
far too coincidental.

203
00:12:00,220 --> 00:12:01,230
The timing?

204
00:12:02,030 --> 00:12:03,930
Seeing her like this the second...

205
00:12:03,990 --> 00:12:06,400
Seung Yun starts coming
to the office really makes me...

206
00:12:07,770 --> 00:12:08,770
Honey.

207
00:12:09,330 --> 00:12:12,000
Honestly, ever since
Seung Yun returned,

208
00:12:12,400 --> 00:12:14,410
Mother has completely pushed...

209
00:12:14,710 --> 00:12:17,740
Do Yun out of her mind,
and it really hurts.

210
00:12:19,410 --> 00:12:20,580
Our Do Yun...

211
00:12:20,950 --> 00:12:23,510
pours himself into the company
day and night.

212
00:12:26,550 --> 00:12:27,890
I think...

213
00:12:28,150 --> 00:12:30,590
we both need an early night tonight.

214
00:12:31,660 --> 00:12:33,290
Let's have a drink
and get some sleep, okay?

215
00:12:34,890 --> 00:12:36,160
Just wait right here.

216
00:12:36,830 --> 00:12:39,230
I'll fetch our very best bottle.

217
00:12:48,940 --> 00:12:49,940
Mother.

218
00:12:51,140 --> 00:12:52,480
You wanted to use today...

219
00:12:53,340 --> 00:12:56,710
to give me a warning,
showing that you can cast aside...

220
00:12:57,350 --> 00:13:00,720
a mere daughter-in-law like me
anytime you want, didn't you?

221
00:13:02,790 --> 00:13:03,790
Fine.

222
00:13:04,860 --> 00:13:06,690
I got your message.

223
00:13:18,100 --> 00:13:20,200
Do you need something?
Can I get you anything?

224
00:13:20,570 --> 00:13:22,510
No, it's fine. I'll get it myself.

225
00:13:23,010 --> 00:13:24,140
Go on in and get some rest.

226
00:13:24,440 --> 00:13:25,580
Are you having a drink?

227
00:13:25,910 --> 00:13:27,710
Should I make you a snack
to go with it?

228
00:13:28,010 --> 00:13:29,050
Too many calories.

229
00:13:29,610 --> 00:13:31,320
I'm just going to have
a quick drink.

230
00:13:31,780 --> 00:13:33,320
I'm fine,
so please go get some rest.

231
00:13:37,990 --> 00:13:39,020
Excuse me, Mrs. Anseong.

232
00:13:39,960 --> 00:13:41,060
Yes, Mr. Cha?

233
00:13:41,830 --> 00:13:43,230
Please don't tell Mother...

234
00:13:43,560 --> 00:13:45,800
that I was drinking.
Keep it between us.

235
00:13:46,260 --> 00:13:49,600
She's already distressed today,
and I don't want to worry her.

236
00:13:50,600 --> 00:13:51,740
I'd appreciate it.

237
00:13:53,640 --> 00:13:54,910
Don't worry, sir.

238
00:14:09,320 --> 00:14:11,490
Dad, what's that?

239
00:14:11,960 --> 00:14:13,060
What? What is it?

240
00:14:20,030 --> 00:14:21,030
Let's see.

241
00:14:21,630 --> 00:14:22,930
(Resident Registration Card:
Kang Da Mi)

242
00:14:23,500 --> 00:14:24,540
This is Kkangda's.

243
00:14:25,040 --> 00:14:26,840
- Why is this here?
- No idea.

244
00:14:27,340 --> 00:14:29,770
Aunt Da Mi said she lost her wallet
and was looking for it.

245
00:14:30,270 --> 00:14:31,310
How strange.

246
00:14:32,210 --> 00:14:35,810
Let's see how much she has in here.

247
00:14:36,680 --> 00:14:37,980
That's it?

248
00:14:38,550 --> 00:14:41,720
She's been working
for how many years now?

249
00:14:41,750 --> 00:14:43,890
And all the cash she has
is three one-dollar bills.

250
00:14:44,960 --> 00:14:46,460
How many do you have, Dad?

251
00:14:47,020 --> 00:14:50,390
Me? Let's see. I have...

252
00:14:52,030 --> 00:14:53,030
Two.

253
00:14:55,670 --> 00:14:57,270
I'm feeling generous, so here.

254
00:14:58,640 --> 00:15:00,900
Why are you putting your money
in Aunt Da Mi's wallet?

255
00:15:01,340 --> 00:15:02,340
What?

256
00:15:03,210 --> 00:15:04,840
Well, that's...

257
00:15:06,240 --> 00:15:09,050
because I'm her big brother.

258
00:15:13,520 --> 00:15:14,520
Grandma.

259
00:15:14,590 --> 00:15:17,120
We found Aunt Da Mi's wallet
on the bench here.

260
00:15:17,520 --> 00:15:18,560
On the bench?

261
00:15:21,990 --> 00:15:22,990
Good grief.

262
00:15:23,060 --> 00:15:25,830
It's a miracle she manages
to hold down a steady job,

263
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:27,430
clumsy as she is.

264
00:15:32,840 --> 00:15:35,510
You didn't take anything
from Da Mi's wallet, did you?

265
00:15:36,610 --> 00:15:38,940
Mom, what kind of person
do you take me for?

266
00:15:39,940 --> 00:15:42,150
I'm truly disappointed.

267
00:15:44,110 --> 00:15:45,480
Su Ah, let's go.

268
00:15:45,920 --> 00:15:46,920
Okay.

269
00:15:47,890 --> 00:15:50,450
If you didn't, fine.
No need to be so dramatic.

270
00:15:55,430 --> 00:15:58,100
Where is Da Mi anyway?
Why isn't she home yet?

271
00:16:12,740 --> 00:16:13,740
Hello?

272
00:16:14,450 --> 00:16:17,850
Hello, Ms. Jeon Jin Hee.
This is Choi Seok Ju,

273
00:16:17,920 --> 00:16:18,980
Team Leader at K Department Store.

274
00:16:19,050 --> 00:16:20,980
Do you have a moment to talk?

275
00:16:22,050 --> 00:16:23,190
Yes, go ahead.

276
00:16:23,620 --> 00:16:26,660
You have been a loyal customer
of our department store for so long,

277
00:16:26,790 --> 00:16:30,330
and causing you such inconvenience
is entirely our fault.

278
00:16:30,430 --> 00:16:32,160
We're currently
checking the facts...

279
00:16:32,160 --> 00:16:34,030
- with the employee and the store...
- No.

280
00:16:34,370 --> 00:16:35,770
There's no need for that.

281
00:16:36,370 --> 00:16:40,100
If it's all right with you,
I would like to apologize in person.

282
00:16:40,300 --> 00:16:41,310
Team Leader Choi.

283
00:16:42,140 --> 00:16:43,740
How many years have I shopped there?

284
00:16:45,810 --> 00:16:48,080
I didn't shop there
just for the merchandise.

285
00:16:48,750 --> 00:16:51,150
I can buy the exact same things
anywhere else.

286
00:16:51,220 --> 00:16:52,850
The reason I shopped
at your store...

287
00:16:54,050 --> 00:16:56,250
is that I was paying
for the treatment...

288
00:16:56,320 --> 00:16:58,690
I received there as well.

289
00:16:58,690 --> 00:17:00,320
Now, however, I see...

290
00:17:01,260 --> 00:17:04,860
that this location doesn't value me
as an important customer...

291
00:17:04,930 --> 00:17:06,700
nearly as much as I thought.

292
00:17:07,100 --> 00:17:08,500
That's not true, ma'am.

293
00:17:08,930 --> 00:17:10,570
Which is all the more reason
why we...

294
00:17:10,770 --> 00:17:11,770
Forget it.

295
00:17:11,940 --> 00:17:13,900
I won't be returning
to that department store.

296
00:17:14,410 --> 00:17:16,110
Ma'am, for a single incident
to end...

297
00:17:16,170 --> 00:17:17,910
our long-standing relationship
like this...

298
00:17:18,110 --> 00:17:20,310
leaves us terribly sorry
and saddened.

299
00:17:20,610 --> 00:17:21,850
If you could give us
just one more chance...

300
00:17:21,910 --> 00:17:23,610
A single mistake...

301
00:17:24,280 --> 00:17:27,150
can turn someone away for good.

302
00:17:31,190 --> 00:17:32,360
Who is it?

303
00:17:35,230 --> 00:17:37,130
I'm not saying this out of anger.

304
00:17:38,460 --> 00:17:39,730
Have a good day.

305
00:17:44,970 --> 00:17:46,270
Did something happen?

306
00:17:48,010 --> 00:17:49,440
Who were you yelling at?

307
00:17:49,840 --> 00:17:50,970
It's nothing.

308
00:17:54,010 --> 00:17:55,050
I'm sorry.

309
00:17:56,410 --> 00:17:57,450
For what?

310
00:17:58,020 --> 00:18:00,080
I should be the one comforting you.

311
00:18:00,880 --> 00:18:02,290
You were right.

312
00:18:02,690 --> 00:18:06,190
I guess work has made me
a little too high-strung lately.

313
00:18:07,220 --> 00:18:09,830
Ever since I completely ruined
that meeting...

314
00:18:09,890 --> 00:18:12,900
with our key investor on day one,
I feel like I've been on edge.

315
00:18:15,270 --> 00:18:17,970
Nobody is perfect all the time.

316
00:18:18,600 --> 00:18:21,670
Everyone feels down sometimes
and gets a bit irritable.

317
00:18:22,370 --> 00:18:24,580
Just remember that
these feelings will pass.

318
00:18:25,210 --> 00:18:26,380
And when that happens...

319
00:18:34,180 --> 00:18:36,990
eating something sweet
is the best cure.

320
00:18:39,060 --> 00:18:41,730
How is it?
Do you feel a little better?

321
00:18:44,230 --> 00:18:45,300
Jeon Jin Hee,

322
00:18:45,960 --> 00:18:49,970
you've done great so far,
and you'll continue to do great.

323
00:18:51,340 --> 00:18:53,640
You've got me by your side,
so what is there to worry about?

324
00:18:55,970 --> 00:18:57,010
You're right.

325
00:18:58,180 --> 00:18:59,240
Just make sure...

326
00:19:00,010 --> 00:19:02,050
you stay by my side forever.

327
00:19:02,980 --> 00:19:04,150
Of course I will.

328
00:19:30,970 --> 00:19:31,980
Here, give it to me.

329
00:19:32,040 --> 00:19:33,840
An older brother
carries these things.

330
00:19:36,010 --> 00:19:37,750
Mom, why are you waiting out here?

331
00:19:38,680 --> 00:19:40,120
How come you two arrived together?

332
00:19:41,990 --> 00:19:44,190
We ran into each other
at the bus stop.

333
00:19:44,520 --> 00:19:46,920
Mom, why are you out here?
Were you waiting for me?

334
00:19:47,390 --> 00:19:48,390
Yes.

335
00:19:48,560 --> 00:19:51,930
- Did you eat yet?
- We did.

336
00:19:52,830 --> 00:19:55,770
Let's go in.
Come on. Let's go inside.

337
00:20:02,170 --> 00:20:03,170
Let's head in.

338
00:20:03,510 --> 00:20:05,610
<i>Come on. Let's go inside</i>

339
00:20:10,010 --> 00:20:12,350
Why is your brother
in such a good mood?

340
00:20:12,750 --> 00:20:13,980
Did he get a promotion?

341
00:20:14,650 --> 00:20:16,650
Well, actually...

342
00:20:18,220 --> 00:20:21,560
I think he managed to resolve
most of his financial troubles.

343
00:20:22,830 --> 00:20:23,830
How?

344
00:20:24,600 --> 00:20:25,730
He said he needed...

345
00:20:25,800 --> 00:20:27,260
at least 200,000 or 300,000 dollars
just to put out the fire.

346
00:20:28,030 --> 00:20:29,070
It was such a huge amount,

347
00:20:29,230 --> 00:20:30,600
so I was worried
and asked him about it.

348
00:20:31,270 --> 00:20:32,840
His company is solid, you know.

349
00:20:33,040 --> 00:20:36,440
It seems he managed to scrape
the money together through work.

350
00:20:37,070 --> 00:20:38,910
So don't worry too much, Mom.

351
00:20:39,880 --> 00:20:40,880
Hey!

352
00:20:40,880 --> 00:20:43,080
Wait, where did you find my wallet?

353
00:20:44,550 --> 00:20:45,720
Gang Nam found it...

354
00:20:46,050 --> 00:20:47,620
on the wooden bench
and gave it to me.

355
00:20:48,320 --> 00:20:50,020
You really need to stop being
so careless.

356
00:20:53,390 --> 00:20:55,930
Right, didn't you say
you wanted to tell me something?

357
00:20:56,490 --> 00:20:57,930
What is it? Tell me now.

358
00:20:58,860 --> 00:21:00,100
Oh, that...

359
00:21:00,460 --> 00:21:01,470
Well...

360
00:21:03,830 --> 00:21:04,840
Never mind.

361
00:21:05,200 --> 00:21:06,970
It doesn't matter anymore.
Let's go in.

362
00:21:07,340 --> 00:21:08,910
What is it?

363
00:21:09,410 --> 00:21:10,970
Don't worry about it.

364
00:21:19,750 --> 00:21:20,780
I knew it.

365
00:21:21,350 --> 00:21:23,650
She was probably going to ask me
to help him with the money.

366
00:21:39,500 --> 00:21:41,610
He went abroad as an expat...

367
00:21:41,670 --> 00:21:44,840
and bragged about
living like a king.

368
00:21:46,610 --> 00:21:49,880
How on earth did he end up
in a semi-basement?

369
00:21:50,950 --> 00:21:52,480
And at 60 years old, no less.

370
00:21:53,680 --> 00:21:55,920
Wretched man.

371
00:21:56,620 --> 00:21:57,620
Well,

372
00:21:58,190 --> 00:22:00,920
water flows
where the channel is carved,

373
00:22:01,090 --> 00:22:03,530
and you reap what you sow.

374
00:22:08,470 --> 00:22:12,200
They should have
rice and kimchi, right?

375
00:22:15,070 --> 00:22:16,740
Who cares?

376
00:22:23,380 --> 00:22:24,780
All right.

377
00:22:32,120 --> 00:22:35,230
We ran out of kimchi ages ago.
Do you even know that?

378
00:22:36,860 --> 00:22:37,860
Please.

379
00:22:38,530 --> 00:22:40,960
I saw you yesterday buying kimchi
from the convenience store...

380
00:22:40,960 --> 00:22:42,730
and chugging soju with it.

381
00:22:43,800 --> 00:22:46,040
Besides, I don't like kimchi.

382
00:22:46,240 --> 00:22:48,510
And Ye Ri barely eats at home.

383
00:22:49,140 --> 00:22:51,540
- I'm off to work.
- Oh, my sweet daughter.

384
00:22:52,440 --> 00:22:54,680
- What? I'm busy.
- It's just...

385
00:22:55,180 --> 00:22:58,150
you look pretty excited today.
What's going on?

386
00:22:58,480 --> 00:23:01,650
Well, Mom, Team Leader Cha Do Yun
called me at the crack of dawn...

387
00:23:01,890 --> 00:23:04,620
and asked me to go with him
to the pop-up store...

388
00:23:04,620 --> 00:23:05,690
where we're sponsoring outfits.

389
00:23:06,320 --> 00:23:07,660
There really is
a lot of inventory today.

390
00:23:07,860 --> 00:23:08,860
See you later.

391
00:23:09,090 --> 00:23:11,130
All right. You got this, sweetie.

392
00:23:11,130 --> 00:23:12,200
I got this.

393
00:23:13,560 --> 00:23:14,560
Hey...

394
00:23:15,700 --> 00:23:18,540
Doesn't that kid even see her dad?

395
00:23:19,400 --> 00:23:20,500
I'm leaving for work too, dear.

396
00:23:21,670 --> 00:23:23,410
You heard what Ye Ri
just said, right?

397
00:23:24,510 --> 00:23:25,880
We need to save up every penny.

398
00:23:26,310 --> 00:23:28,350
That way, we can at least
rent an apartment.

399
00:23:30,250 --> 00:23:31,410
Sunglasses too?

400
00:23:32,220 --> 00:23:35,050
Gosh, you're really trying hard.

401
00:23:36,920 --> 00:23:38,320
Whatever it takes to make money.

402
00:23:50,530 --> 00:23:52,200
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

403
00:23:53,170 --> 00:23:55,540
I'm going through menopause?

404
00:23:56,170 --> 00:23:58,710
Someone as gorgeous
and elegant as me?

405
00:24:00,210 --> 00:24:03,250
Back in the day,
when I was the rice cake shop girl,

406
00:24:03,480 --> 00:24:06,020
everyone in the neighborhood
said I put Audrey Hepburn to shame.

407
00:24:07,550 --> 00:24:11,120
By the way, when is Dr. Ju
going to show up?

408
00:24:22,470 --> 00:24:24,600
Good morning.

409
00:24:36,750 --> 00:24:38,050
Goodness...

410
00:24:39,780 --> 00:24:40,780
Oh, my.

411
00:24:42,050 --> 00:24:44,020
I didn't know you were there.

412
00:24:44,520 --> 00:24:46,620
Good morning, Dr. Ju.

413
00:24:48,230 --> 00:24:49,390
Do you sweep the alley...

414
00:24:50,560 --> 00:24:52,230
every day like this?

415
00:24:53,100 --> 00:24:54,100
You work so hard.

416
00:24:54,200 --> 00:24:57,300
I should start coming out earlier
to help you sweep from now on.

417
00:24:58,470 --> 00:25:02,670
Goodness, you don't need
to go out of your way like that.

418
00:25:03,610 --> 00:25:05,640
Not at all.
I'll just come in a bit earlier.

419
00:25:07,140 --> 00:25:09,910
Then I'll see you tomorrow morning.

420
00:25:09,980 --> 00:25:13,220
I always come out and sweep...

421
00:25:13,550 --> 00:25:15,350
at 9:30 a.m. sharp, Dr. Ju.

422
00:25:17,390 --> 00:25:18,560
Understood. See you then.

423
00:25:24,690 --> 00:25:27,230
(Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine)

424
00:25:28,900 --> 00:25:30,900
Oh, yes!

425
00:25:41,510 --> 00:25:44,480
Right, Jaden Cha called me earlier.

426
00:25:45,050 --> 00:25:46,280
What could it be about?

427
00:25:52,820 --> 00:25:54,560
Min Hee, what's wrong?

428
00:25:55,290 --> 00:25:56,290
Da Mi,

429
00:25:57,560 --> 00:25:58,900
what should I do?

430
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:02,100
What happened?

431
00:26:04,230 --> 00:26:07,140
What?
Calm down and tell me everything.

432
00:26:08,510 --> 00:26:10,840
Why is your contract
not getting renewed?

433
00:26:16,210 --> 00:26:17,210
What?

434
00:26:29,230 --> 00:26:30,630
Hello.

435
00:26:30,630 --> 00:26:33,630
I'm Kang Da Mi, manager
at K Department Store's VIP Luxury Hall.

436
00:26:36,030 --> 00:26:38,070
I'm the CEO's designated
personal shopper.

437
00:26:38,640 --> 00:26:41,340
I came to see her
about an urgent matter.

438
00:26:41,470 --> 00:26:42,970
Please let me in.

439
00:26:43,240 --> 00:26:44,440
Do you have an appointment?

440
00:26:45,310 --> 00:26:46,380
I don't,

441
00:26:47,240 --> 00:26:50,550
but I'm not allowed to
contact the CEO first.

442
00:26:52,120 --> 00:26:53,420
Still, I really need to see her.

443
00:26:53,950 --> 00:26:56,090
Could you please tell her I'm here?

444
00:26:57,290 --> 00:26:59,460
I'm sorry,
but without an appointment,

445
00:26:59,460 --> 00:27:00,560
I can't let you in.

446
00:27:01,060 --> 00:27:02,190
Please, I'm begging you.

447
00:27:02,830 --> 00:27:05,930
Could you just call the CEO's office
and let her know I'm here...

448
00:27:06,230 --> 00:27:08,730
and would like to see her,
even briefly?

449
00:27:09,970 --> 00:27:11,000
Isn't she...

450
00:27:12,040 --> 00:27:13,570
the girl from the department store?

451
00:27:14,870 --> 00:27:16,610
I'm sorry, but I can't.

452
00:27:21,240 --> 00:27:22,280
Let her in.

453
00:27:26,020 --> 00:27:27,050
Goodness...

454
00:27:27,980 --> 00:27:29,490
She's also my personal shopper.

455
00:27:30,220 --> 00:27:32,160
I'll let CEO Jeon know myself.

456
00:27:35,990 --> 00:27:38,560
This is a surprise, Kang Da Mi.
How have you been?

457
00:27:52,640 --> 00:27:54,610
(Mission: Mompossible)

458
00:28:14,630 --> 00:28:17,330
You said you needed
200,000 or 300,000 dollars right away.

459
00:28:17,330 --> 00:28:18,470
Is that not enough?

460
00:28:18,470 --> 00:28:20,900
Sir, could you please tell us...

461
00:28:20,970 --> 00:28:22,840
your repayment plan
for the overdue principal?

462
00:28:23,010 --> 00:28:25,610
It's admirable that you're fighting
for your junior colleague's job,

463
00:28:25,710 --> 00:28:28,010
but from now on,
you'd better read the room...

464
00:28:28,010 --> 00:28:29,180
before charging in.

465
00:28:30,650 --> 00:28:32,650
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
